  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Cove Light",
    "description": "A red-and-white lighthouse and its keeper's cottage on a rock out in the water, with a little harbour of its own: the rock wraps round a sheltered cove where the rowing boat ties up at stone steps. There is no bridge; the boat is the only way there. The lantern and windows light up after dark in World View. 29 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Rock** — seven dark Block 2x2s in a U, three along the back and two down each side, make a rock 6 by 4 with a cove in the middle open to the south. Rocks sit round the outside.\n2. **Steps** — at the head of the cove, two stone Wide Stairs, turned 270° (press **R** three times) so they climb north, the upper one on a Brick 1x2, lead up out of the water onto the middle of the back.\n3. **Boat** — a blue Plate 2x4 hull nosed into the cove at the foot of the steps, a Bench across it for the seat, and two Trims for oars, turned 90°.\n4. **Cottage** — a white Block 2x2 on the west end of the back with a red Gable Roof 2x2. Its Door, turned 90°, opens onto the top of the steps; a Small Window looks out over the cove and glows with lamplight at night.\n5. **Tower** — two Block 2x2s, white and red, on the east end, its Door facing the cottage's across the landing. A Small Window in the red band glows at night.\n6. **Lantern** — a Round Plate 2x2 for the gallery, a Lantern that lights up after dark, and a red Cone Roof.\n\nStand it out in open water, away from the shore, so the boat is the only way there.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Rock: 7 Block 2x2, 4 Rock\n- Steps: 2 Wide Stair, 1 Brick 1x2\n- Boat: 1 Plate 2x4, 1 Bench, 2 Trim\n- Cottage: 1 Block 2x2, 1 Gable Roof 2x2, 1 Door, 1 Small Window\n- Tower: 2 Block 2x2, 1 Door, 1 Small Window\n- Lantern: 1 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Cone Roof\n\n29 bricks in all.\n",
